package cajeta.lang;

/**
 * A total ordering over values of type `T`. Modeled on `java.lang.Comparable`.
 *
 * `compareTo` returns a negative int32 if `this` orders before `other`, zero if
 * they order equally, and a positive int32 if `this` orders after `other`. The
 * ordering must be total and consistent: `a.compareTo(b)` and `b.compareTo(a)`
 * must report opposite signs, and the relation must be transitive.
 *
 * Implementors that also define equality (`operator==`) should keep the two
 * consistent — `a == b` iff `a.compareTo(b) == 0` — though cajeta does not
 * enforce this.
 *
 * ## Implementing
 *
 * An implementor returns a signed `int32` by comparing its ordering fields. The
 * `cajeta.time` value types — `Duration`, `LocalDate`, `LocalDateTime`,
 * and `ZonedDateTime` — follow this pattern. `Duration`, for example, orders
 * by its total nanosecond field:
 *
 * ```cajeta
 * public int32 compareTo(Duration other) {
 *     if (this.nanos < other.nanos) {
 *         return -1;
 *     }
 *     if (this.nanos > other.nanos) {
 *         return 1;
 *     }
 *     return 0;
 * }
 * ```
 *
 * ## Note (toolchain)
 *
 * Templated-interface vtable instantiation for implementing classes is still
 * maturing in the compiler, so the `cajeta.time` value types declare `compareTo`
 * as a concrete method and call it directly (monomorphic dispatch) rather than
 * relying on virtual dispatch through this interface. The interface is the
 * documented contract and the seam for generic ordered algorithms once those
 * vtables land.
 */
public interface Comparable<T> {
    /**
     * Orders `this` against `other`: negative if `this` sorts first, `0` if they
     * sort equally, positive if `this` sorts last. Must be total, transitive, and
     * sign-symmetric with `other.compareTo(this)`.
     *
     * Here two `LocalDate` values are ordered chronologically:
     *
     * ```cajeta
     * stack LocalDate a = LocalDate.of(2026, 6, 5);
     * stack LocalDate b = LocalDate.of(2026, 12, 25);
     * if (a.compareTo(b) < 0) {
     *     // a is earlier than b
     * }
     * ```
     */
    int32 compareTo(T other);
}
